WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
They are still mechanical sound
waves, even though those frequencies

00:00:01.302 --> 00:00:03.323
lie outside typical human hearing

00:00:04.131 --> 00:00:07.957
Some elephants communicate using
very low frequency rumbles, and

00:00:07.958 --> 00:00:11.845
detectors can measure infrasound
from storms or volcanic activity

00:00:12.554 --> 00:00:16.606
Yes, but that does not establish
a reliable animal-based

00:00:16.666 --> 00:00:17.971
earthquake warning system.

00:00:18.556 --> 00:00:21.524
Interesting observations need
strong evidence before we turn

00:00:21.524 --> 00:00:22.893
them into safety predictions

00:00:23.236 --> 00:00:26.722
An echo is reflected, sound
heard after the original.

00:00:27.166 --> 00:00:29.595
Hard surfaces often reflect strongly.

00:00:29.936 --> 00:00:34.151
Soft furnishings can absorb some
sound energy and reduce reverberation.

00:00:34.618 --> 00:00:38.033
Why do distance calculations
contain a division by two?

00:00:38.828 --> 00:00:41.946
Because the timed pulse travels
out to the reflector and back.

00:00:42.416 --> 00:00:46.887
Speed times return time gives the whole
journey, not the one-way distance.

00:00:47.727 --> 00:00:48.519
Exactly.

00:00:48.838 --> 00:00:52.777
If an echo returns after zero point
five seconds and sound speed is

00:00:52.779 --> 00:00:56.868
three hundred and forty meters per
second, how far away is the reflector?

00:00:57.618 --> 00:01:00.195
Total distance is one
hundred and seventy meters.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.905
Half of that is eighty-five meters.

00:01:03.476 --> 00:01:07.228
Forgetting the return trip would double
my answer and possibly lose a mark.

00:01:08.014 --> 00:01:09.068
Nicely rescued.

00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:13.494
Sonar applies this principle in water
using the appropriate speed there.

00:01:14.075 --> 00:01:18.461
Medical ultrasound uses reflections from
tissue boundaries to help build an image.

00:01:19.237 --> 00:01:21.036
Ultrasound is not an X-ray.

00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:25.509
It does not use ionizing radiation,
but medical equipment should still be

00:01:25.511 --> 00:01:27.733
operated appropriately by trained people.

00:01:28.391 --> 00:01:29.097
Exactly.

00:01:29.462 --> 00:01:33.768
Non-ionizing does not mean unlimited
exposure is automatically harmless.

00:01:34.198 --> 00:01:37.493
Ultrasound can also be used in
controlled cleaning equipment.

00:01:37.957 --> 00:01:41.418
The applications depend on how
the waves interact with materials.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:46.062
Final rescue: Name four
pairs we must keep separate.

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:48.968
Pitch depends mainly on frequency.

00:01:49.214 --> 00:01:51.625
Loudness relates to
amplitude and perception.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.272
Period is time.

00:01:53.494 --> 00:01:54.985
Wavelength is distance.

00:01:55.309 --> 00:01:57.858
Particles oscillate while
the disturbance travels.

00:01:58.319 --> 00:02:01.581
Echo return distance is twice
the distance to the reflector.

00:02:02.391 --> 00:02:04.615
That is a clear scientific performance.

00:02:04.949 --> 00:02:09.089
Read the axes, include units,
use the correct medium speed,

00:02:09.264 --> 00:02:10.558
and keep your ears safe.

00:02:10.886 --> 00:02:13.598
No standing ovation needs
to be painfully loud
